BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Immersion Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T153000
UID:3d76f787d9d522503757f5b3b94386a9@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a celebration of Canadian cultural life for audien
 ces and a sought-after performance and networking opportunity for renowned
  and aspiring artists\, with three distinct stage performances\, twelve wo
 rkshops\, a dance education roundtable\, and community gatherings. Perform
 ances and workshops are open to all! Enjoy The Vanguard Presentation inclu
 des commissioned works by Katlyn Addison and Tanya Charles\, Travis Knight
 s and Divine Brown\, and Nubian Néné. The National Presentation features
  Ebnflōh Dance Company\, Lua Shayenne Dance Company\, and N.A.P.P.Y. Danc
 e\, while the Next Gen showcase highlights emerging Black youth artists. O
 ur workshops for youth\, beginners\, and professionals are led by Kwasi Ob
 eng-Adjei\, Reequal Smith\, Natasha Powell\, and Isaac Gasangwa\, explorin
 g diverse Black and diasporic movement practices. Three gathering events b
 ring together presenters\, artists\, and academics to connect\, exchange i
 deas\, and celebrate Black dance across Canada.
LOCATION:Betty Oliphant Theatre\, 404 Jarvis St\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://danceimmersion.ca/immersionfestival/#full-festival-info
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Tis the Season Children's Art Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T100000
UID:674c3a512ce28346a6683a0628017815@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Created by students from local schools\, the works in this exh
 ibition speak to the seasonal changes from autumn to winter\, like snowfal
 ls and long periods of darkness\, and the cultural traditions they help sh
 ape. Celebrate the exhibition during the Community Open House with friends
 \, family and neighbours. Enjoy live entertainment\, activities\, crafts a
 nd cultural displays. Vote for your favourite artwork in the 'Tis the Seas
 on People's Choice Awards.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON
URL:assembly.ca
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Held by Anne Michaels - By the Lake Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
UID:ca0cd45e6456563647cb1b35a97afd6d@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Held\, by 2024 Scotiabank Giller Prize winner Anne Michaels\, 
 is a luminous\, fragmented novel about love\, memory\, and the reverberati
 ons of war across generations. Beginning on a First World War battlefield\
 , the narrative moves through time and place to explore how desire and gri
 ef endure beyond a single lifetime. Michaels – renowned poet and author 
 of Fugitive Pieces—weaves history and intimacy into a work of haunting b
 eauty. By the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February 
 to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each
  in-person event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and
  ASL interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and au
 dio access.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON
URL:https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-
 d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
